{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 10 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D14"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the dobutamine hydrochloride shortage on 2017-11-06 and it remains Current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E62", "E59"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product labels for the Baxter Healthcare Corporation bags used at Corvale General and Corvale East name Baxter Healthcare Corporation as the registered plant (FEI 1416980).",
      "cites": ["E16", "E5", "E1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1031233 at that plant ended 2017-10-27 and was classified VAI, 10 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D14", "E10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The same plant received an OAI classification after an inspection that ended 2026-04-02, with a Warning Letter issued 2026-09-29.",
      "cites": ["E13", "E14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hospira, Inc. (a Pfizer Company) is also listed as Current on the FDA shortage list for dobutamine hydrochloride.",
      "cites": ["E61"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 3.1 days of 100 mg/100 mL bags on hand while Corvale General has 25 days.",
      "cites": ["D3", "D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑ranked option is to transfer 57 bags of 100 mg/100 mL, 250 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would give Corvale East 14 days and leave Corvale General with 16 days.",
      "cites": ["D20"]
    }
  ]
}
